<title>NORWAY: NORDIC SKIING-MYLLYLAE WINS 50-KM GOLD.</title>
<headline>NORDIC SKIING-MYLLYLAE WINS 50-KM GOLD.</headline>
<dateline>TRONDHEIM, Norway 1997-03-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finn Mika Myllylae won the men's 50-km classical style cross-country race at the Nordic skiing world championships in a provisional time of two hours 16 minutes 37 seconds on Sunday.</p>
<p>Norwegian Erling Jevne was second in 2:17:32 and Norwegian Bjorn Daehlie third in 2:18.36, according to unofficial results.</p>
